#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:52
msgid ""
"link:{url_wiki}/Initiatives/Git_Forge_Initiative_2025[Git Forge 2025 "
"Initiative] Lead: link:{url_wiki}/User:Ryanlerch[*Ryan Lerch*]"
msgstr ""
"Ansvarig för "
"link:{url_wiki}/Initiatives/Git_Forge_Initiative_2025[initiativet Git Forge "
"2025]: link:{url_wiki}/User:Ryanlerch[*Ryan Lerch*]"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Ryan has been involved with Fedora since 2008, contributing across many "
"different teams including docs, infrastructure, and design.  He was a "
"founding editor of Fedora Magazine and has been involved in various Fedora "
"projects over the years.  He currently leads the Git Forge Initiative, "
"working to consolidate Fedora's source code management, issue tracking, and "
"project hosting onto a single Forgejo platform deployed on Fedora "
"Infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"Ryan har varit engagerad i Fedora sedan 2008 och har bidragit till många "
"olika grupper, bland annat dokumentation, infrastruktur och design.  Han var"
" en av grundredaktörerna för Fedora Magazine och har genom åren deltagit i "
"flera Fedora-projekt.  Han leder nu Git Forge Initiative och arbetar för att"
" samla Fedoras källkodshantering, ärendehantering och projekthosting på en "
"enda Forgejo-plattform som körs i Fedora Infrastructure."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:58
msgid ""
"link:{url_wiki}/Initiatives/Fedora_Docs_2025[Fedora Docs 2025 Initiative] "
"Co-Leads: link:{url_wiki}/User:Pboy[*Peter Boy*] & "
"link:{url_wiki}/User:Pbokoc[*Petr Bokoč*]"
msgstr ""
"Medansvariga för link:{url_wiki}/Initiatives/Fedora_Docs_2025[initiativet "
"Fedora Docs 2025]: link:{url_wiki}/User:Pboy[*Peter Boy*] och "
"link:{url_wiki}/User:Pbokoc[*Petr Bokoč*]"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:63
msgid ""
"Peter is involved with Fedora since FC1, working with desktop and especially"
" Server and contributing to documentation in the early days.  After a break "
"of several years, in 2020, he got involved in revitalizing and improving the"
" Fedora Server Edition.  From 2022 onwards, he was also involved in setting "
"up a new Docs Team and improving the Fedora documentation.  Currently, he is"
" also co-lead of the Fedora Docs 2025 Community Initiative."
msgstr ""
"Peter har varit engagerad i Fedora sedan FC1, arbetat med skrivbordet och "
"särskilt Server samt bidragit till dokumentationen under de tidiga åren.  "
"Efter ett uppehåll på flera år engagerade han sig 2020 i att återuppliva och"
" förbättra Fedora Server Edition.  Från 2022 deltog han också i att bygga "
"upp ett nytt Docs Team och förbättra Fedoradokumentationen.  Han är nu även "
"medansvarig för gemenskapsinitiativet Fedora Docs 2025."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:65
msgid ""
"Petr is a technical writer on the xref:cle::index.adoc[Community Linux "
"Engineering] team who has been active in xref:fedora-docs::index.adoc[Fedora"
" Documentation] since 2013, mostly working on user-facing documentation such"
" as the Release Notes, the old (now no longer published) Installation Guide,"
" and Quick Docs."
msgstr ""
"Petr är teknisk skribent i gruppen xref:cle::index.adoc[Community Linux "
"Engineering] och har arbetat med xref:fedora-docs::index.adoc[Fedora "
"Documentation] sedan 2013, främst med användarinriktad dokumentation som "
"Release Notes, den gamla installationshandboken som inte längre publiceras "
"och Quick Docs."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:67
msgid ""
"link:{url_wiki}/Initiatives/Initiatives/Fedora_bootc[Fedora bootc "
"Initiative] Lead: link: {url_wiki}/User:Nimbinatus[*Laura Santamaria*]"
msgstr ""
"Ansvarig för "
"link:{url_wiki}/Initiatives/Initiatives/Fedora_bootc[initiativet Fedora "
"bootc]: link: {url_wiki}/User:Nimbinatus[*Laura Santamaria*]"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/members.adoc:74
msgid ""
"As a Community Architect at Red Hat, Laura loves to learn and explain how "
"things work to bridge the gaps in engineering disciplines.  She is or has "
"been the host of a number of podcasts on topics from technical leadership to"
" cloud native technology and has held many different roles within and "
"outside of tech.  As a community member, she co-hosts multiple meetups in "
"the Austin, Texas, area, including Cloud Austin.  For many years, she taught"
" Python for the Women Who Code Austin meetup, as well.  She is an organizer "
"for DevOpsDays Austin and PyTexas and advises KCD Texas, all community-run "
"conferences, as well as a global core co-chair for the DevOpsDays community."
"  For the past number of years, she has been a returning program committee "
"member for Open Source Summit’s Cloud Open track that explores cloud "
"infrastructure and cloud apps.  Outside of tech, Laura runs, reads, and "
"watches clouds—the real kind."
msgstr ""
"Som Community Architect på Red Hat tycker Laura om att lära sig och förklara"
" hur saker fungerar för att överbrygga klyftor mellan tekniska områden.  Hon"
" är eller har varit programledare för flera poddar om allt från tekniskt "
"ledarskap till molnbaserad teknik och har haft många olika roller inom och "
"utanför teknikbranschen.  Som medlem i gemenskapen är hon medarrangör för "
"flera träffar i Austin, Texas, bland annat Cloud Austin.  Under många år "
"undervisade hon också i Python på träffarna Women Who Code Austin.  Hon "
"arrangerar DevOpsDays Austin och PyTexas och är rådgivare åt KCD Texas, som "
"alla är konferenser drivna av gemenskapen, samt global vice ordförande för "
"DevOpsDays-gemenskapen.  De senaste åren har hon återkommande varit medlem i"
" programkommittén för Open Source Summits spår Cloud Open, som behandlar "
"molninfrastruktur och molnprogram.  Utanför teknikvärlden springer Laura, "
"läser och tittar på moln – riktiga moln."

